From: Zakk <zakk@gentoozh.org>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:40:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: replace a same-radio link sta in rhash

The link sta table is keyed by address per device. A client that
authenticates on a second vif of the same radio, while hostapd still
holds it on the first, failed station add with -EEXIST until the old
entry timed out, because only an entry of another radio was replaced.
Replace the existing entry whatever its radio.

Signed-off-by: Zakk <zakk@gentoozh.org>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -7253,11 +7253,12 @@ static int ath12k_mac_station_add(struct
 	/*
 	 * In case of Split PHY and roaming scenario, pdev idx
 	 * might differ but both the pdev will share same rhash
-	 * table. In that case update the rhash table if link_sta is
+	 * table. A client may also move to another vif of the same
+	 * radio. In both cases update the rhash table if link_sta is
 	 * already present
 	 */
 	temp_arsta = ath12k_link_sta_find_by_addr(ab, arsta->addr);
-	if (temp_arsta && temp_arsta->arvif->ar != ar)
+	if (temp_arsta)
 		ath12k_link_sta_rhash_delete(ab, temp_arsta);
 
 	ret = ath12k_link_sta_rhash_add(ab, arsta);
